{"id": "EUVD-2026-48819", "enisaUuid": "0fad3cdb-75cf-3fda-ac6c-f0180e860155", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvfio/pci: Release the VGA arbiter client on register_device() failure\n\nThe re-order in the Fixes commit below displaced vfio_pci_vga_init() as\nthe last failure point of what is now vfio_pci_core_register_device()\nwithout introducing an unwind for the VGA arbiter registration.\n\nIn current kernels this is mostly benign because vfio_pci_set_decode()\nonly uses pci_dev state, but the original failure path could leave a\ncallback with a freed vdev cookie.  The stale registration also becomes\nunsafe again once the callback follows drvdata to the vfio device.\n\nAdd the required VGA unwind callout.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:51:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:36", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f2a35a0c7ea7da347b814750eaa78adf3582381", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d65decde9afd2bd78bcfffdc0df73b82a0b5509", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef4c38d30b3744e89eb5048218904bb629ea8d47", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e0a3f642e607848669235f5069f35640abbfc88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42d758a09d2c46c42357ecde9a5492f015bde2e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52adb2dff7ce3d8430e2bdc5988b618a430def85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/278a5659c391fe5afe5f9ce1bad1fd24e90144f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/daedde7f024ecf88bc8e832ed40cf2c795f0796a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64475", "GHSA-mj56-4c42-9869"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01724be2-c7fa-3d5f-b199-67cc20e9155e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11.21 <5.12"}, {"id": "05a6ddf0-5e58-392a-a715-e05936ee9b0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4aeec3984ddc853f7c65903bde472ffdef7